
# One predicate that must hold of a record. `hold` is the language's existing word for a constraint, with the
# shape the code role already gives it: a name and a list of `bind` children.
#
#   hold is-equal
#     read self/kind
#     text <vowel>
#
#   hold is-within
#     bind self, read self/symbol
#     bind other, text <aeiou>
#
# `self` is the record under test, which is the language's own meaning of `self`. Every other read reaches a
# `host`. Arguments are positional (`slot`) or named with the predicate's own parameter names (`bind`), and
# mixing the two in one `hold` is an error.
#
# Which predicates a field accepts is declared per field by the query catalog, and one the resolver cannot push
# down to an index is refused. See note/term/view/03-find.md.

load @term/mill/code/view/seed/mine
  find view-seed
  find view-bind

mine view-hold
  mine term, term hold
    site name
    mine list
      mine any
        mine form, like view-bind
          site bind
        mine form, like view-seed
          site slot
